@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.component.form_section a ds:Component;
    ds:name "Form Section";
    ds:summary "Form Section groups related settings in a named semantic region. It renders a generated-id `h2` beside the consumer `children` in a two-column CSS grid, then stacks the heading above the content when the section container becomes narrower than the columns’ combined minimum widths.\n\nUse it for settings groups whose controls are conceptually related but are not one native checkbox/radio fieldset. Consecutive Form Section siblings receive a theme-aware divider and vertical separation; a lone or first section does not.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.form_section\n  semantic: section\n  a11y:\n    labelled-by: generated heading id\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: responsive grid\n        styles:\n          layout.display: grid\n          layout.columns: minmax(19rem, 24rem) minmax(28rem, 1fr)\n          spacing.gap: $spv--large $sph--x-large\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              semantic: h2\n              role: section heading\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              role: settings content\n              styles:\n                size.min-width: 0\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n                slotName: children\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=25-54&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 28\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Settings grouping**\n\nUse to divide a settings surface into labelled groups of related controls.\n\n**Responsive heading layout**\n\nUse when the heading should sit beside content when space allows and stack above it in constrained containers.\n\n**Discoverable page regions**\n\nUse when the section should appear as a named region in the accessibility tree and the surrounding heading hierarchy expects a level-two heading.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Checkbox or radio semantics**\n\nA group of mutually exclusive choices that need fieldset and legend.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Form Section instead of fieldset/legend for choice groups.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a native fieldset with legend for radio and checkbox groups, or use Expandable Radio Group.\n\n**Unlabelled spacing**\n\nUsing the component merely to add visual spacing or dividers.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Rendering a Form Section without a meaningful title just to add a divider or grid.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use Vanilla utility classes or a dedicated divider/spacing component; every section requires a purposeful title.\n\n**Arbitrary heading levels**\n\nA heading hierarchy where `h2` would create skipped or flattened levels.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Form Section in a context where the heading hierarchy would be broken (e.g., after an h3).\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a different component or restructure the page heading hierarchy; the current API does not expose heading-level control.\n\n**General card or field group**\n\nDecorative card layout or a generic field wrapper without semantic region meaning.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Form Section as a replacement for arbitrary cards or field containers.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a plain styled div with Vanilla classes, or use a semantic section only when it represents a named page region.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Preserve the section, h2, and aria-labelledby relationship generated by the component.\n- The named `<section>` is exposed as a region; use enough sections to aid navigation, not so many that landmark/region navigation becomes noisy.\n- Keep heading levels logical in the surrounding page. The fixed `h2` cannot be changed through props.\n- The component adds no focus target or keyboard behavior; focus remains on interactive children.\n\n### Content\n\n- Use a short noun phrase that describes the settings in the section.\n- Keep unrelated controls in separate sections and avoid sections containing only one trivial field.\n- Localize `title` and child content at the call site; there are no source-owned visible strings.\n\n### Internationalization\n\n- Allow longer translated headings to wrap. The heading column has a 19rem minimum in wide mode and stacks when the full grid no longer fits.\n- Do not encode meaning only through the small-caps visual treatment; the semantic heading text must remain clear in every locale.\n\n### Keyboard navigation\n\n- The section itself adds no tab stop; child controls retain normal document order.\n- Grid presentation does not change DOM order: the heading precedes `children` in both layouts.\n\n### Device and layout\n\n- The breakpoint follows the section’s own inline size, not viewport width, so navigation or side panels can trigger stacking.\n- Wide mode requires the 19rem label minimum, horizontal gap, and 28rem content minimum. At or below their combined threshold the grid becomes one `minmax(0, 1fr)` column.\n- Content receives `min-width: 0` so descendants can shrink, but consumers remain responsible for responsive child controls and overflow.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "title";
        ds:summary "Content rendered in the `h2`; its generated id labels the section. ";
        ds:propertyType "node";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `ReactNode`. Keep it textual and concise. Interactive or complex content can produce an unsuitable heading/region name. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "children";
        ds:summary "Composition slot rendered in the content column.";
        ds:propertyType "node";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `ReactNode`. Maintain logical reading and focus order; `null` is type-compatible React content but leaves an empty named section. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "className";
        ds:summary "Merged onto the root section with the local class.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:constraints "Consumer CSS can affect layout or semantics; preserve the container and label relationship. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ].
